      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <limits>\n#include <memory>\n\nclass FastInput {\n    static constexpr std::size_t buffer_size = 1 << 16;\n    char buffer[buffer_size];\n    std::size_t position = 0;\n    std::size_t available = 0;\n\n    int next_char() {\n        if (position == available) {\n            available = std::fread(buffer, 1, buffer_size, stdin);\n            position = 0;\n            if (available == 0) {\n                return EOF;\n            }\n        }\n        return static_cast<unsigned char>(buffer[position++]);\n    }\n\npublic:\n    bool read_int(int& value) {\n        int c;\n        do {\n            c = next_char();\n            if (c == EOF) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        } while (c <= ' ');\n\n        bool negative = false;\n        if (c == '-') {\n            negative = true;\n            c = next_char();\n        }\n\n        unsigned int result = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            result = result * 10u + static_cast<unsigned int>(c - '0');\n            c = next_char();\n        }\n        value = negative ? -static_cast<int>(result) : static_cast<int>(result);\n        return true;\n    }\n};\n\nstatic int maximum_serial(const int* horizontal, int n, int s, int width) {\n    const int height = n - s + 1;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> vertical(new int[width]);\n    for (int column = 0; column < width; ++column) {\n        vertical[column] = 0;\n    }\n\n    for (int row = 0; row < s; ++row) {\n        const int* source = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * width;\n        for (int column = 0; column < width; ++column) {\n            vertical[column] += source[column];\n        }\n    }\n\n    int maximum = std::numeric_limits<int>::min();\n    for (int column = 0; column < width; ++column) {\n        maximum = std::max(maximum, vertical[column]);\n    }\n\n    for (int top = 1; top < height; ++top) {\n        const int* leaving = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * width;\n        const int* entering = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * width;\n        for (int column = 0; column < width; ++column) {\n            const int value = vertical[column] + entering[column] - leaving[column];\n            vertical[column] = value;\n            maximum = std::max(maximum, value);\n        }\n    }\n    return maximum;\n}\n\nstatic int maximum_parallel(const int* horizontal, int n, int s, int width) {\n    const int height = n - s + 1;\n    constexpr int chunks = 4;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> vertical(new int[width]);\n    int maximum = std::numeric_limits<int>::min();\n\n#if defined(_OPENMP)\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(max : maximum)\n#endif\n    for (int chunk = 0; chunk < chunks; ++chunk) {\n        const int begin = width * chunk / chunks;\n        const int end = width * (chunk + 1) / chunks;\n\n        for (int column = begin; column < end; ++column) {\n            vertical[column] = 0;\n        }\n        for (int row = 0; row < s; ++row) {\n            const int* source = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * width + begin;\n            for (int column = begin; column < end; ++column) {\n                vertical[column] += *source++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int column = begin; column < end; ++column) {\n            maximum = std::max(maximum, vertical[column]);\n        }\n\n        for (int top = 1; top < height; ++top) {\n            const int* leaving = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * width + begin;\n            const int* entering = horizontal + static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * width + begin;\n            for (int column = begin; column < end; ++column) {\n                const int value = vertical[column] + *entering++ - *leaving++;\n                vertical[column] = value;\n                maximum = std::max(maximum, value);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return maximum;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    FastInput input;\n    int n;\n    int s;\n    if (!input.read_int(n) || !input.read_int(s) || n <= 0 || s <= 0 || s >= n) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const int width = n - s + 1;\n    const int height = width;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> horizontal(new int[static_cast<std::size_t>(n) * width]);\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> row(new int[n]);\n\n    for (int r = 0; r < n; ++r) {\n        for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n            input.read_int(row[column]);\n        }\n\n        int running = 0;\n        for (int column = 0; column < s; ++column) {\n            running += row[column];\n        }\n        int* destination = horizontal.get() + static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * width;\n        destination[0] = running;\n        for (int column = 1; column < width; ++column) {\n            running += row[column + s - 1] - row[column - 1];\n            destination[column] = running;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t windows = static_cast<std::size_t>(width) * height;\n    const int answer = windows < (1u << 17)\n        ? maximum_serial(horizontal.get(), n, s, width)\n        : maximum_parallel(horizontal.get(), n, s, width);\n    std::printf(\"%d\\n\", answer);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A staged O(N^2) box-filter eliminates the baseline's S-factor work; a static four-way OpenMP column partition gives each thread contiguous strips, private vertical state, and a deterministic max reduction while avoiding per-row synchronization.",
